{"name":"Inverness","hex":"#576238","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Inverness","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the administrative centre of Highland council area, Scotland.","A rural locality in the Shire of Livingstone, Queensland, Australia."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of overcoat constructed without sleeves and having a shoulder cape extending to the wrists. The best examples are quite heavy, made from Harris tweed; often associated with Sherlock Holmes.","A variation of this coat, the \"coachman's cape\": the shoulder cape does not extend around the back but is made of two segments, the length of each being sewn into the seam of the coat on either side."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Inverness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inverness","blocks":[{"text":"Inverness is a city in the Scottish Highlands in the north of Scotland. Long regarded as the de facto capital of the Scottish Highlands, it is the administrative centre for The Highland Council region whose headquarters are located close to the city centre. A regional hub for healthcare, education and research, business and economic services, public administration, culture, music and entertainment, media, communications, transport and leisure, the city provides a range of services for the wider Highlands and Islands Region, a large hinterland encompassing a population of around half a million people and an area of some 39,911 km² or 51% of Scotland's total landmass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness","wikidata":"Q160493"},{"title":"Inverness (provincial electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Inverness is a provincial electoral district on Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia, Canada, that elects one member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Inverness_provincial_electoral_district.svg/330px-Inverness_provincial_electoral_district.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness_(provincial_electoral_district)","wikidata":"Q6060198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg/500px-Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg/1280px-Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg/500px-Panoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanoramic_view_of_Inverness.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Inverness_Public_Library_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3421847.jpg/500px-Inverness_Public_Library_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3421847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Inverness_Public_Library_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3421847.jpg/500px-Inverness_Public_Library_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3421847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInverness_Public_Library_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3421847.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_Tollbooth_Steeple_%2827411318711%29.jpg/500px-The_Tollbooth_Steeple_%2827411318711%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped